WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.830
The tiny carnivorous snowmen are relentless
- sharp fangs dripping with blood, as they

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:11.540
crawl en masse towards the Mobile Task Force,
opening fire on them with assault rifles.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.820
Who would have guessed that a mere hour or
two earlier, a young boy was joyfully playing

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.630
around in the snow here?

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:21.750
How had things gone from frosty to freaky
so fast?

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.910
Let’s rewind the clock…

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:28.670
There was a chill in the air, that lingering,
biting cold that would gnaw at your exposed

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:33.960
skin if you dared to step outside in anything
less than a thick, warm coat for protection.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:40.030
The ground was still coated in a heavy snowfall,
a holdover from Christmas just passed, weather

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:44.800
that had refused to let up well into the early
days of the New Year.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.190
Everyone reaches an age where the cynicism
of life, the weight of expectations that keep

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:54.950
you anchored in the real world, they all coalesce
to rob you of the childlike wonder at the

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.950
snow.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:01.420
As you get older, the snow loses its novelty,
it becomes a source of inconvenience, something

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:04.619
you need to shovel off the driveway to take
your car out.

00:01:04.619 --> 00:01:09.890
Whereas, turn the clock back to youth, and
it’s like a tiny miracle, it coats your

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:16.680
whole world in a clean blanket of freezing
frosting, turning the ordinary into a wonderland.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.461
Robert and Mikaylah Anderson were glad that
their son, Michael, was still at an age where

00:01:21.461 --> 00:01:23.850
he could enjoy the snow.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:28.549
After all, Mikaylah getting to take her son
out in his sled or seeing him hurling snowballs

00:01:28.549 --> 00:01:33.290
at Robert was able to provide them with a
little bit of warmth during the freezing cold,

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.220
snowier months in Missouri.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:40.650
Optimism was never enough to melt the snow,
however, and maybe that’s what drew in those

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:41.909
creatures…

00:01:41.909 --> 00:01:43.320
the snowmen.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:48.030
It was early 2019, not even a full two weeks
into the year.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:52.350
By now, Michael had gotten used to the fact
that after Christmas and New Year’s Day,

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.560
a begrudging return to school would soon follow.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:02:00.689
As much as it clearly brought down his mood,
nothing lifted his spirits like still getting

00:02:00.689 --> 00:02:02.590
to be out in the snow.

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:07.060
And after a long day of helping his mom take
down the tinsel and pack up the lights while

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.170
his dad disposed of the tree, Michael was
itching to get outside.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:16.650
“Please, Mom?” he begged as a box of decorations
was placed back in the attic; his hands clasped

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.430
together in a pleading gesture.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:19.580
“Please, please, please!

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:23.700
Just five minutes, I won’t go further than
the front yard!”

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.900
Mikaylah sighed, partly from exhaustion, but
a smile crept onto her face; it was hard not

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:31.670
to find her son’s love for the snow endearing.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:34.320
“Alright, but only for five minutes!”

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.430
she insisted firmly.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:39.610
“And I want to see gloves, hat, and scarf,
not just a coat, mister!”

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:43.990
With the speed and excitement that she and
her husband had long since lost, she watched

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:46.989
Michael race off to gather his warmest winter
coat.

00:02:46.989 --> 00:02:48.769
“Remember when we were like that?”

00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:53.000
Robert heaved a sigh as he appeared from chopping
up the dried-out, dehydrated remains of the

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.000
Christmas tree.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.390
“No, do you?”

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:57.620
Mikaylah replied with a light chuckle.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:02.319
Before long, Michael had donned his gloves
and coat, almost a size too big.

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:07.100
His scarf was almost wrapping up his entire
head, save for the bobble hat that poked out

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.209
at the top.

00:03:08.209 --> 00:03:13.080
Robert opened up the front door, and his son
stepped out into a world that had been whitewashed

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.599
with clear, cold snow.

00:03:15.599 --> 00:03:19.870
Given that the Andersons lived on a small
street in Grain Valley, there weren’t many

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:25.549
other people around, especially not with another
flurry of snowfall moving closer in the clouds

00:03:25.549 --> 00:03:26.660
up above.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:30.580
But it wasn’t the next snowfall that the
residents of Grain Valley, Missouri, should

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:36.290
have been worrying about; it was the previous
one, the one that had already fallen… and

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:40.930
what was now hiding among the snow in the
Anderson family’s front yard.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:44.930
Having few other kids his own age to play
with, and not being allowed to venture too

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:50.010
far from the front porch, Michael was content
to spend his precious time outdoors making

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:53.230
snow angels, or practicing throwing snowballs.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:57.939
He had long been trying to get one to clear
the roof of the small house he and his parents

00:03:57.939 --> 00:04:02.629
shared, leaving a few scattered patches of
snow embedded on the roof shingles.

00:04:02.629 --> 00:04:05.939
A few meters from the front door stood a snowman.

00:04:05.939 --> 00:04:11.150
Granted, that was hardly a rare sight at this
time of year, especially in the cold weather.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:15.540
But what was so unusual about it was, that
Michael hadn’t remembered making a snowman

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.549
recently.

00:04:16.549 --> 00:04:20.670
His parents hadn’t let him out in the snow
on his own since the start of the New Year,

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:25.030
given how badly the downfall and icy winds
had been for the first week of January.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:29.660
Sure, somebody else could have made it, taking
a pause as they passed by the Anderson’s

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:30.660
front yard.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:34.860
Although, not Michael nor either of his parents
had spotted anyone doing that.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:39.910
The snowman itself was featureless, the white
of its ice-cold body smeared with mud and

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:45.500
dead leaves, debris that had been packed in
with the snow used in its crude construction.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.250
It was featureless too.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:51.810
Whoever had made it hadn’t gone to the effort
of giving it a face, nor draped an old scarf

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.773
over it, or given it a hat.

00:04:53.773 --> 00:04:59.050
It just stood there, but not like any other
snowmen; there was nothing welcoming about

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:00.050
it.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:02.620
In fact, it was, fittingly, cold.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:07.940
Given how far away it stood, it was almost
as if it was watching the house.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.360
Curiously, Michael began to approach the snowman.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:15.520
Being only nine years old, his imagination
was immediately running with the possibility

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:20.890
that this snow and mulch construct could be
alive, much akin to the likes of Frosty the

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:21.910
Snowman.

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:26.530
Little did young Michael Anderson know that
he wasn’t far from the truth, although this

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:32.810
particular snowman wasn’t quite the happy,
jolly soul from the much-covered holiday song.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:36.610
He hadn’t gotten that much closer to the
snowman when he heard something move nearer

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:37.790
to where he stood.

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:42.760
There was the rustle of leaves and the snapping
of small twigs coming from a bush next to

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:43.760
him.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:48.250
Michael couldn’t see what it was, but it
was far too low to the ground and too close

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:50.430
to the house for it to be a bird.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:55.380
Maybe a possum or raccoon had gotten trapped
in the thin branches and was now scrabbling

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.010
to try and free itself.

00:05:57.010 --> 00:06:01.080
Diverting from approaching the snowman, he
walked closer to the plant.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:04.630
As he did, the rustling got louder, more frantic…
almost hungry.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:10.490
There wasn’t just one creature lurking out
of sight beneath the leaves, but lots of somethings…

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:14.680
Robert and Mikaylah had been sitting indoors
watching the TV when they heard a spine-chilling

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.280
scream coming from outside.

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:20.410
Instantly, they were both up on their feet,
racing towards the front door.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:24.500
Robert threw it open, and Michael dashed inside
in floods of fearful tears.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:25.820
“What happened, sweetie?”

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.690
Mikaylah asked concerned, brushing snowflakes
from her son’s coat.

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:29.690
“Are you okay?

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:30.690
Did you slip over?”

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:35.350
Through crying and sniffling, shaking uncontrollably
with how afraid he was, Michael couldn’t

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:36.960
find the words to answer.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:41.990
Instead, he pointed through the still-open
door, directly at the snowman, still standing

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:43.479
at the edge of the front yard.

00:06:43.479 --> 00:06:45.400
“How long has that been there?”

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.870
Robert wondered aloud, taking a single step
outside.

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:49.169
“Don’t, Dad!”

00:06:49.169 --> 00:06:50.220
Michael screamed.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.009
But it was already too late…

00:06:52.009 --> 00:06:55.160
Something small and speedy had leaped out
of the snow in the front yard and latched

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:56.599
onto Robert’s leg.

00:06:56.599 --> 00:07:01.759
He howled as he felt searing pain, bitten
by rows of tiny, pointed teeth as sharp as

00:07:01.759 --> 00:07:04.879
needles and as bitterly cold as ice.

00:07:04.879 --> 00:07:09.009
Stumbling back, Robert Anderson fell over
and landed on the floor of the front hallway,

00:07:09.009 --> 00:07:12.479
inadvertently carrying whatever had attacked
him into his home.

00:07:12.479 --> 00:07:17.110
Both Mikaylah and Michael screamed in fear
as the tiny creature clawed its way up Robert’s

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:22.200
leg while he swatted at it frantically, trying
to brush it away before it could get closer.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:26.120
With a blind swipe of his hand, he knocked
the creature to the floor and clambered to

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:31.800
his feet, arms outstretched, keeping his wife
and son behind him, while staring in disbelief

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.600
at what had bitten him.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:37.710
It was barely more than half a meter tall,
a tiny, white…

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:38.729
snowman.

00:07:38.729 --> 00:07:43.960
Bulbous, bloodied eyes bulged from its head,
much like those of an insect.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:49.319
Directly between the eyes was a hole, a mouth
not unlike a lamprey, lined with rows of sharp

00:07:49.319 --> 00:07:51.240
teeth that all pointed inwards.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:56.020
It reared up and lunged toward the Anderson
family in a display of aggression that caused

00:07:56.020 --> 00:08:00.090
all three of them to jump, warily backing
away from the snow creature.

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:04.110
It was then that Robert and Mikaylah noticed
what had frightened their son so much.

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:07.949
Out of the corner of their eye, they both
simultaneously caught sight of the open front

00:08:07.949 --> 00:08:10.449
door, and the yard beyond.

00:08:10.449 --> 00:08:15.470
Wriggling through the snow, shifting it as
they moved, were even more of the creatures,

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:19.380
slithering towards the house like piranhas
catching the scent of blood in the water.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:25.000
And standing ominously just beyond the driveway
was the snowman, as if it was a general commanding

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.680
its troops to storm the house.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:31.960
The Andersons raced upstairs as the swarm
of snow creatures came spilling into the house,

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:36.729
crawling from the yard onto the floor and
piling on top of each other like ants to climb

00:08:36.729 --> 00:08:37.780
the stairs.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:42.180
Naturally, Mikaylah’s first instinct – as
well as protecting her son – was to call

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:43.180
the police.

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:47.300
While Robert held the door to their bedroom
shut, Mikaylah held Michael close and pleaded

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:50.510
with the local Grain Valley Police Department
to come and help them.

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:55.480
Although, they only seemed to take the call
seriously when Michael started screaming again;

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:59.500
one of the snow creatures had pushed its way
under the doorframe and was snaking its way

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:03.910
towards Robert to attack him, leaving a trail
of water behind it.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:09.080
Stepping back and thinking fast, Robert grabbed
a hairdryer and switched it on full blast.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:12.810
The sudden rush of electrically heated air
caused the toothy snow creature to retreat

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:14.500
into a corner.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:17.920
Refusing to let up, Robert got closer and
kept the hairdryer trained on it, eventually

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:22.220
causing the creature to melt until little
more was left than a damp puddle.

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:26.589
But the victory was momentary; there were
still more of them crawling up the stairs

00:09:26.589 --> 00:09:28.140
after the Andersons.

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:31.730
With their sharp teeth, they were gnawing
at the wood of the bedroom door, trying to

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:34.100
force their way inside…

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:38.370
Fortunately for Robert, Mikaylah, and their
son Michael, they wouldn’t be able to recall

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:42.390
the horrific events of January 12th, 2019,
for much longer.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:46.510
By the time the local police arrived, it had
become clear to the officers responding that

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:50.620
they were well out of their depth, especially
when one of them was injured, suffering a

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:52.230
bite from a snow creature.

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:57.470
This was what led to the SCP Foundation being
called in, and within fifteen minutes, they

00:09:57.470 --> 00:10:01.220
had dispatched Mobile Task Force operatives
to secure the anomaly.

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:04.950
Being some of the Foundation’s most highly
trained agents, it didn’t take long for

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:07.980
the MTF to neutralize the carnivorous snow
creatures.

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:12.970
However, they quickly realized that the mysterious
snowman that had seemingly spawned the swarm

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:18.380
could not be melted by any conventional means,
nor would it deteriorate naturally on its

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:19.380
own.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:23.120
A cover story was issued that Michael had
suffered an accident and fallen down an open

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:26.660
pothole that had become obscured by heavy
snowfall.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:30.650
As a result, police officers were dispatched
to help him - although the injury sustained

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:35.010
by one officer due to a bite from a snow creature
was never explained.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:39.230
Following this, the Anderson family was administered
amnestics, meaning they quickly forgot about

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:41.600
the whole terrifying ordeal.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:46.570
Maybe it was for the best, however, young
Michael seemed irreparably changed.

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:51.260
He never went out to enjoy the snow again,
repeatedly suffering from nightmares about

00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:52.260
the cold.

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:56.900
Meanwhile, the anomalous snowman was recovered
and thus designated as SCP-4230.

00:10:56.900 --> 00:11:02.639
Immediately, the SCP Foundation did as their
organization does best and commenced testing,

00:11:02.639 --> 00:11:05.519
with a human subject, no less.

00:11:05.519 --> 00:11:10.320
They quickly discovered that SCP-4230 seemed
to generate a sort of field around itself,

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:16.110
that could trigger a distinctive physiological
change in any human being or animal that came

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.410
within six meters of the snowman.

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:23.560
This process became known under the designation
of SCP-4230-1.

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:27.740
It appeared that Michael Anderson had managed
to unknowingly escape this fate purely by

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:33.770
not getting too close to SCP-4230, staying
just far away enough so as not to trigger

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:36.370
SCP-4230-1.

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:42.540
The Foundation placed, D-19375, a member of
their D Class personnel, within this six-meter

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:47.630
radius of the snowman, and observed the gradual
changes he underwent over the following week.

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:53.450
For simplicity’s sake, we’ll refer to
D-19375 as ‘Frost’ a rather fitting moniker,

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:55.930
and you’ll soon see why.

00:11:55.930 --> 00:12:00.070
Within a day of exposure to the snowman, Frost
complained to a Senior Researcher that he

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:05.440
felt a lot colder than usual, although he
exhibited no other observable symptoms, beyond

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:08.370
the coughing and sniffling of a common cold.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:13.220
By the following day, Frost was far worse
for wear, appearing to have lost significant

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:16.710
body mass to the point where he appeared to
have been malnourished.

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:20.810
His cold-like symptoms had continued, accompanied
by disorientating dizziness.

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:26.880
And, as if all that wasn’t bad enough, his
skin tone had seemingly lost its natural pigment,

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:30.870
reduced to an unnaturally pale shade, as white
as snow.

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:35.300
Day three saw Frost’s body continue to change
rapidly at an alarming rate.

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:39.430
He was internally producing an unknown chemical
that looked to be responsible for enacting

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:43.920
certain alterations, namely the dissolving
of his femur and fibula.

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:48.190
The cold and dizziness were also now made
all the worse by the addition of pain to the

00:12:48.190 --> 00:12:49.889
man’s lower body.

00:12:49.889 --> 00:12:54.240
Frost even reported to Foundation researchers
studying him that every movement he was able

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:58.430
to make caused him to suffer extreme levels
of physical pain.

00:12:58.430 --> 00:13:03.630
But yet, rather than attempt to cure his condition,
the Foundation apathetically observed, noting

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:07.650
down the process of SCP-4230-1.

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:13.560
Within five days of exposure to SCP-4230,
naturally occurring substances within Frost’s

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:16.300
body had traveled downwards and solidified.

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:22.240
This was then followed by the most shocking
stage of SCP-4230-1 process so far, and one

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:28.400
that made the Foundation realize that these
weren’t just changes: it was a transformation.

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:33.510
When day five saw Frost’s skeleton physically
reshaping itself, his head becoming a sphere

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:38.300
and his arms extending outwards like brittle
twigs, it soon became clear what was happening

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:42.420
to him: he was turning into a snowman.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:48.360
Rendered immobile and blind, a week after
SCP-4230-1 began to take effect, Frost had

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:51.070
started to secrete an unknown substance.

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:55.560
This liquid lowered his body temperature,
freezing almost instantly, and turning his

00:13:55.560 --> 00:14:01.209
skin into an icy, white mass… worryingly
similar to snow.

00:14:01.209 --> 00:14:07.710
Sure enough, on the eighth day, the extent
of the SCP-4230-1 process was made evident.

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:12.930
Frost had already perished, his body now looking
identical to a plain, featureless snowman,

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:17.210
no eyes or face, just a blank, cold slate.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:21.930
But underneath the outer layer of snow, Frost’s
bones and the rest of his organs were still

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:23.770
contained inside.

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:28.649
From the outside, though, he wasn’t even
human anymore, just an instance of what became

00:14:28.649 --> 00:14:34.370
known as SCP-4230-A.
However, being turned into another snowman

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:38.570
by close proximity to SCP-4230 wasn’t even
the worst part…

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:43.320
By now, you might be wondering ‘what were
those snow creatures that attacked the Andersons?’.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:47.790
You’d be forgiven for thinking that perhaps
these were rodents or other wild animals affected

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:53.639
by SCP-4230-1; after all, testing has shown
that the process doesn’t just alter human

00:14:53.639 --> 00:14:54.940
physiology.

00:14:54.940 --> 00:15:01.620
But these carnivorous, needle-toothed creatures
are known as SCP-4230-Bs, and they’re nasty

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:03.870
little critters, to say the least.

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:09.699
When a person – or animal – is turned
into a snowman during SCP-4230-1, becoming

00:15:09.699 --> 00:15:14.079
one of these instances is far from the full
extent of the transformation.

00:15:14.079 --> 00:15:19.250
The tests the Foundation conducted on Frost,
and presumably on numerous other D class personnel

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:24.560
as well, led to them discovering the further
alterations made when something becomes an

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:27.649
SCP-4230-A instance.

00:15:27.649 --> 00:15:33.700
Their freezing, snow-encased bodies become
hosts for white, spherical eggs.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:39.960
After a subject like Frost becomes an SCP-4230-A
snowman, these eggs will hatch within seventy-two

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:45.930
hours, producing up to nineteen instances
of SCP-4230-B creatures.

00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:50.470
The Foundation was quick to examine these
bizarre snow spawn, gathering up as many as

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:52.010
they could for testing.

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:57.940
They found that instances of SCP-4230-B matured
to adulthood remarkably quickly, reaching

00:15:57.940 --> 00:16:01.060
adulthood in fifteen seconds.

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:04.259
Destroying the eggs containing these creatures
seemed to be an effective way of preventing

00:16:04.259 --> 00:16:10.340
swarms of SCP-4230-Bs from getting loose,
although the snowman each egg came from would

00:16:10.340 --> 00:16:13.470
also have to be destroyed to achieve this
result.

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:18.670
Also, the lifespans of the smaller snow creatures
only lasted for a total of twenty-four hours,

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:25.399
and they would melt away after a full day
of life, regardless of the surrounding temperature.

00:16:25.399 --> 00:16:29.079
SCP-4230-Bs seemed uninterested in food that
was presented to them.

00:16:29.079 --> 00:16:33.570
Specifically, one test involved giving a snow
creature a head of lettuce and a watermelon.

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:37.790
The creature regarded the fruit and vegetable
with little interest, even refusing to eat

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:40.550
either despite prompts from the researchers.

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:46.410
This painted the SCP-4230-Bs as exclusive
carnivores, which explained why they attacked

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:52.420
the Anderson family: they were trying to eat
them, hunting the Andersons as a pack.

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:57.649
Further testing into SCP-4230-Bs revealed
they had a weakness to heat above a temperature

00:16:57.649 --> 00:16:59.899
of forty degrees Fahrenheit.

00:16:59.899 --> 00:17:05.390
During another test, a D Class was sent into
a cell with ten of the carnivorous snow creatures,

00:17:05.390 --> 00:17:10.709
armed only with a simple lighter, an emergency
flare, and one gallon of gasoline.

00:17:10.709 --> 00:17:16.530
Immediately, all ten of the SCP-4230-Bs crawled
towards the man, hungry and determined him

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:18.550
as a new source of food.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:21.430
That is, until they noticed the lighter he
was carrying.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:25.829
The D Class frantically clicked at the spark
wheel, until the flame danced from the lighter,

00:17:25.829 --> 00:17:29.630
causing seven of the creatures to back away
from the heat source cautiously.

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:33.919
The D Class was able to kill the remaining
three instances in self defense, causing them

00:17:33.919 --> 00:17:35.350
to melt with little effort.

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:39.540
He was far luckier than the subject of the
next test would be…

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:43.260
Another D Class was placed in a holding cell
with three of the snow creatures, and much

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:47.580
like before, they instantly acknowledged his
presence and began approaching him.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:52.039
However, the Foundation had sent this member
of D Class in completely unarmed, without

00:17:52.039 --> 00:17:55.010
even so much as a match to defend himself.

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:59.690
The carnivorous beasts made short work of
their helpless victim, feeding on what was

00:17:59.690 --> 00:18:00.690
left.

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:05.690
The Foundation was able to dispatch instances
of SCP-4230-B with relative ease.

00:18:05.690 --> 00:18:10.250
Even without waiting for them to simply melt
after a day, the use of flamethrowers or drawing

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:14.750
them into warmer areas seemed effective enough
at destroying the small snowmen that hatched

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:17.320
out of SCP-4230-A bodies.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:22.610
However, some bright spark at the Foundation
decided to test what would happen if the opposite

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:27.169
element was used against SCP-4230-B creatures.

00:18:27.169 --> 00:18:32.150
Were they vulnerable to the snow despite being
made from a snow-like substance themselves?

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:36.640
Another test was conducted to answer this,
which involved a small snowball being thrown

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:39.780
at one of the SCP-4230-Bs.

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:44.210
The result of that incident has been entirely
expunged from the Foundation’s archives,

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:46.299
but it’s a safe guess as to why.

00:18:46.299 --> 00:18:52.860
Evidently, when attacked using snow or ice,
SCP-4230-Bs are seemingly able to adapt in

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:55.530
some way that is detrimental to their attacker.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:59.390
Do they add snow to their mass, or become
even more aggressive?

00:18:59.390 --> 00:19:04.360
It’s hard to say, given the redactions,
but the results of that final test were deemed

00:19:04.360 --> 00:19:11.470
so catastrophic that the Foundation banned
any further testing that involved SCP-4230-Bs.

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:16.870
As for where SCP-4230 first came from, the
Foundation is still baffled.

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:20.930
The first reported incident involving the
killer snowman and the carnivorous creatures

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:27.950
it produced came when the Andersons found
themselves under siege by hungry SCP-4230-Bs.

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:33.530
Maybe the snowman is just a freak of nature,
or the result of an unknown pathogen or microorganism

00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:36.409
carried in on a snowstorm one fateful night.

00:19:36.409 --> 00:19:41.789
Or perhaps SCP-4230 is something far, far
more vicious.

00:19:41.789 --> 00:19:46.429
Whatever the case, we would recommend waiting
for the sun to come back out and the snow

00:19:46.429 --> 00:19:49.200
to melt… just to be safe.

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:55.540
Now go and check out “SCP-4666 THE YULE
MAN” and “SCP -784 CHRISTMAS CHEER”

00:19:55.540 --> 00:20:00.510
for more anomalous absurdity from the time
of the year when the weather outside is delightful,

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:02.900
but for the Foundation, things are truly frightful.

